Dulcamara: a new sound channel is made while the mixer waits.

check_channel grows the channels (realloc) as a game first uses one, a movie's or its mask's among them, without
the audio lock, while the mixer (callback) goes through them on its own thread: when realloc moves them, the mixer
reads freed memory. Dulcamara's own host tests crashed on it as they made many channels at once while sound played.
The growth now takes the audio lock (LOCK_AUDIO, SDL's: recursive). Applied to Ren'Py 8's src/renpysound_core.c and
Ren'Py 7's module/renpysound_core.c, the same there.

--- a/renpysound_core.c
+++ b/renpysound_core.c
@@ -610,8 +610,12 @@
     }
 
     if (c >= num_channels) {
+        /* Dulcamara: the mixer (callback) goes through the channels as it plays, on its own thread: they may move
+         * (realloc) only while it waits. SDL's mutexes are recursive, so a caller that holds it already may call. */
+        LOCK_AUDIO();
         struct Channel *extended_channels = realloc(channels, sizeof(struct Channel) * (c + 1));
         if (extended_channels == NULL) {
+            UNLOCK_AUDIO();
             error(RPS_ERROR);
             error_msg = "Unable to allocate additional channels.";
             return -1;
@@ -632,6 +636,7 @@
         }
 
         num_channels = c + 1;
+        UNLOCK_AUDIO();
     }
 
     return 0;
